Subject: [PATCH 4/4] RISC-V: Add instruction patterns for 32-bit multiply-add
 and bit-extract fusion.

This patch adds instruction patterns to support fusion of multiply-add
and bit extraction sequences for the ARC-V RHX-100 processor.  This
increases the likelihood that fusible sequences are produced in more
situations.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/riscv/arcv-rhx100.md (arcv_rhx100_imul_fused): New
	reservation.
	(arcv_rhx100_alu_fused): New reservation.
	* config/riscv/iterators.md (is_zero_extract): New code attribute.
	* config/riscv/riscv.cc (riscv_rtx_costs): Reduce the cost of
	zero_extract when RISCV_FUSE_BFEXT fusion is enabled.
	* config/riscv/riscv.md (*<any_extract:optab><GPR:mode>3): Disable
	the generic split when RISCV_FUSE_BFEXT fusion is enabled.
	(maddhisi4): Expand to a fused multiply-add when RISCV_FUSE_MULT_ADD
	fusion is enabled.
	(umaddhisi4): New expand.
	(madd_fused): New insn_and_split.
	(madd_fused_extended): New insn_and_split.
	(*zero_extract_fused): New insn_and_split.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/riscv/arcv-fusion-limm-condbr.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/arcv-fusion-madd.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/arcv-fusion-xbfu.c: New test.

Co-authored-by: Artemiy Volkov <artemiyv@acm.org>
Co-authored-by: Michiel Derhaeg <michiel.derhaeg@globalfoundries.com>
Signed-off-by: Luis Silva <luis.silva@globalfoundries.com>

===

Changes since v1:
  - Gate the new patterns and the zero_extract cost on the generic
    fusion flags (riscv_fusion_enabled_p (RISCV_FUSE_BFEXT) /
    RISCV_FUSE_MULT_ADD) instead of TARGET_ARCV_RHX100, so any tune that
    enables those flags can use them.
  - Moved the imul_fused/alu_fused "type" attribute addition out of this
    patch into the scheduling patch, so riscv.md no longer touches the
    type list here.
  - madd_fused_extended now wraps the SImode inputs of the *_extended
    adds with gen_lowpart (SImode, ...) for correct RV64 codegen.
  - ChangeLog fixes: the new insns are named madd_fused /
    madd_fused_extended (v1 listed madd_split / madd_split_extended), and
    the iterators.md attribute is is_zero_extract.
